# Rows of a world database built from dummy-content's preset interior
# plugin (one exterior cell, one interior cell and their load-door pair)
# through the default in-house reader. Every table is listed, including
# empty ones. One line per row: table|column=value|column=value.
# Rows are sorted by column values before formatting, so SQLite row order
# and HashMap iteration cannot churn. NULL is NULL, text is a JSON string,
# a REAL shows nine decimals when that token parses back to the same
# value and Rust's round-trip form otherwise, and a BLOB is
# blob:<sha256 prefix>:<length>.
# Normalized columns, because the machine or clock sets them:
#   conversion_cache.plugin_path: the fixture's temporary directory, which differs between runs and machines
#   conversion_cache.last_converted: the wall-clock time when the cache row was written
#   record_overrides.source_path: the plugin path in the fixture's temporary directory
# Omitted objects, named so no exclusion is silent:
#   exterior_spatial_node (shadow): R-tree node block of exterior_spatial
#   exterior_spatial_parent (shadow): R-tree parent block of exterior_spatial
#   exterior_spatial_rowid (shadow): R-tree rowid map of exterior_spatial
#   lod_chunks_spatial_node (shadow): R-tree node block of lod_chunks_spatial
#   lod_chunks_spatial_parent (shadow): R-tree parent block of lod_chunks_spatial
#   lod_chunks_spatial_rowid (shadow): R-tree rowid map of lod_chunks_spatial
# The virtual tables exterior_spatial and lod_chunks_spatial are included:
# their rows are the published spatial index. The test fails if the omitted
# set differs from this list.
